						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16505#msg16505"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16505#msg16505">Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2724 on:</b> April 16, 2005, 09:12:29 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							so many guilds had drama over Qvic its really funny.&nbsp; i remember when Assent first got into Qvic their guild leadership was caught farming them late at night when the guild was told not to or something of that effect and they had to changed the rules where if mobs where 1-groupale they couldnt be for dkp or something like that.&nbsp; i found it amusing, and at the same time i&#039;m very happy with how my guild did Qvic molds.&nbsp; dkp-free, could farm them any time you wanted too, because they where easy, and better equiped guildies helps the guild more then dkp drama blah blah blah.&nbsp; also the guild paid for every mold the guild made which helped alot of the poorer members out.<br /><br />but at the same time if a guild decides to have items, like Qvic molds cost dkp it makes sense that they wouldnt encourage farming durring off-hours because there would be no real way to enforce the dkp and stuff... and thats just a drama boat waiting to happen!<br /><br /><br />im not really sure what i&#039;m trying to say here as i&#039;m alittle drunk but i hate you all so its ok.
						</td>
